    "title": "Tim Corbin: Vanderbilt baseball coach still went to Omaha in 2020",
    "text": "VANDERBILTThere's wasn't a College World Series in 2020, but Tim Corbin went to Omaha anyway | Estes Gentry EstesNashville TennesseanFeb. 18, 2021Updated Feb. 19, 2021, 8:39 p.m. CTYou can take the coach out of the College World Series, but you can’t take the CWS out of …Well, you get the idea.To illustrate, though, let’s go back to the summer. The COVID-19 pandemic dealt Vanderbilt baseball coach Tim Corbin a rare travel opportunity. With a season canceled, no recruiting tasks and basically “nothing to do,” Corbin and his wife packed up and hit the road. It was “the first time I’d taken a non-baseball-related trip in my life,” he said.",
